// Proactive English C1 · Syria Edition · Book 1 · Unit 12 — Answer Key
const L = require('./lib');
const { p, h1, h2, pb, sp, box, table, C } = L;
const out = [];
const S = (t) => p(t, { bold: true, color: C.teal, before: 160, after: 60 });
const A = (t) => p(t, { indent: 200, after: 50 });
const SAMPLE = (paras) => box('Sample answer', paras, 'FFFFFF', C.navy);
const NOTE = (t) => box('Note', [t], C.lyellow, C.orange);

out.push(h1('Unit 12  What the Year Made Automatic — Answer Key'));
out.push(p('_Proactive English · C1 · Book 1 · Syria Edition · Answer Key_', { color: '7F7F7F' }));
out.push(box('How to use this key', [
  'Every task has an answer or a **full sample**. **No model in this book contains a sentence about its own writing**, and the two declared exceptions in Book 1 are 1.6 and 24.1.',
  '⚠ **This is the last unit of Book 1 and it is the only one in which the subject matter is the class itself.** **Everything in it is a claim a student makes about their own writing, and the whole unit exists to make those claims checkable** — **which means that the cycle fails the moment the room is allowed to say _I am more careful_ and sit down.** **Expect to refuse about a third of the first answers in 12.1, and say in advance that you are going to.**',
  '⚠ **Peer review stays at band 2 and this is the sixth and last unit of it.** **Band 2 is _name the reader, then name what is absent — an absence and not an error_** — **and in this unit the reader is almost always the student themselves in September, which is the hardest reader in the book to name without reproaching.**',
  '**What to collect before 12.1, and chase it hard, because two of the three cannot be substituted.** ⚠ **One:** the student\'s **own _cannot yet_ list from 1.2, in the handwriting they wrote it in.** **Two:** one document of theirs **from September or October** and one **from June or July**, for 12.7. **Three:** a document they have actually sent, for the invisibility test in 12.4. **Three or four students will have lost the 1.2 list**: they reconstruct it, in September\'s words, marked as reconstructed, and the reconstruction is itself worth something — **a reconstructed list and a real one differ in a way the room can see.**',
  '**12.7 carries the last examination papers in Book 1.** **Reading and Use of English Part 5** is multiple choice on a text, six items at two marks each; **Writing Part 2** is the proposal; **Listening Part 4** is multiple matching with two tasks over five speakers.',
  '⚠ **And the sentence to say in 12.1 and not to repeat: nobody is being assessed in this unit.** **A student who believes the readiness page goes to anybody will write it to be read well, and a readiness page written to be read well is worthless to the teacher who gets it in September.** **Say that the only readers are the student and their next teacher, and that four minutes is all it will get** — **which is the honest figure and the one that makes the page short.**',
], C.lblue, C.navy));

// ===================== 12.1 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('12.1  The move you no longer notice'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **Write the ten claims on the board and leave the second column empty, and do not comment on any of them.** **In most classes seven or eight of the ten first answers are a feeling** — _I am more careful_, _I think about the reader_ — **and the empty column is the whole of the cycle.** **Do not fill it in for anybody.** **The board as it stands after five minutes is the evidence that the cycle is needed, and a teacher who improves two of the claims on the way round has destroyed it.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Evidence: **1** and **4**. ⚠ **1 is a dated act** — _on 4 May I deleted the word "significant" before anybody asked me to_ — **and 4 is a dated negative with a denominator**: _in June a referee asked me nothing about my search, for the first time in four submissions._ **2, 3 and 5 are feelings**, and all three were as true last June as this one, which is the sentence to say to the room. **The question that turns any of the three into evidence is the same one and it is four words: _when was the last time?_**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — ⚠ **an occasion with a date**: something that happened, or did not happen, on a day you can name.'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** **He filed eighty-six words on 11 June and the desk ran them unchanged, which had never happened before and has happened four times since.** ⚠ **It surprised him because he had not decided anything**: he found that he had started with the shape and the holes about three weeks after he stopped thinking about it, so the noticing came after the change.   **2** ⚠ **They cannot be checked by anybody, including the person making them** — **and _I am more careful_ is true of everybody in the room every June and was true last June as well.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The empty second column is the design of this cycle and it only works once, so do not explain it in advance.** **Ask for one sentence, write the ten claims, and then ask which two of the five in 1b are evidence.** **The room will see its own board.** **In this class eight of the ten first claims were feelings and the two that were not came from Mr Shihabi and Dr Qabbani** — **and Dr Qabbani\'s was a negative, which is the form nobody expects to be told is the strongest.** ⚠ **Do not let a student rewrite their board claim until after 1b.** **The value of the exercise is the gap between what they said and what they then recognise as evidence, and a corrected board has no gap in it.**'));
out.push(NOTE('**The three forms of occasion, and the order of difficulty, measured across this class.** ⚠ **A starting is easiest** — **a date and an act.** **A negative is the strongest and the room does not believe it until it is shown one** — _nobody asked me, for the first time in four submissions_, **which is 4.5 turned inwards.** **A stopping is the hardest to produce and the easiest to recognise**, because nobody notices the day they stop, **and the way to date one is to go back through your own documents until you find the last instance.** ⚠ **That search is the homework and it has taken between twenty minutes and two hours in this class and has never failed.** **Say the two hours out loud.** **A student who expects it to take five minutes abandons it at fifteen.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** **A starting, with its date** — _on 2 May I wrote the limitation under the claim it limits, which I had not done before._   **2** **A stopping, dated by its last instance** — _my last "significant" is in a document of 4 March and there has not been one since._   **3** **A negative with a denominator** — _in June a referee asked me nothing about my search, for the first time in four submissions._   **4** ⚠ **No occasion yet, and the honest form is _I can do it and I still decide to_** — **which is a true answer and not a weaker one.**   **5** ⚠ **Noticed afterwards, and say so** — _I noticed in June that I had stopped writing sentences first, about three weeks after it started._ **The change was not a decision and cannot be claimed as one.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** **Evidence.** **A dated act, and the _before anybody asked me to_ is what makes it a move rather than a correction.**',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **Feeling.** **Question: _when was the last time you were not?_**',
  '**Row 3** **Evidence.** **A stopping, dated by its last instance** — **7 February, and the sentence is complete without any claim about what it means.**',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **Feeling.** **Question: _when was the last time you did not write to a senior person because of how it would read?_**',
  '**Row 5** **Evidence, and the strongest on the card.** ⚠ **A count, a date and a _for the first time_** — **which is a denominator in four words.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card B)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** **Evidence.** **A negative.** ⚠ **B should ask for the denominator** — _out of how many submissions?_ — **because the negative is only strong with it.**',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **Feeling.** **Question: _when was the last time your formal English let you down, and what was the document?_**',
  '**Row 3** **Evidence.** **A stopping with its last instance** — **March**, **and the phrase is one the room will recognise, which makes the row the easiest on either card.**',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **Feeling, and the hardest to refuse because it sounds technical.** **Question: _when did you last hedge something and then take the hedge out?_**',
  '**Row 5** **Evidence.** **Three letters since April with no formula at the top** — **a count with a period, and a stopping stated as a count.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3R · Perform – listener task'));
out.push(A('**Rows 2 and 4 on both cards are feelings and the question is always the same: _when was the last time?_** ⚠ **Make the room produce that question out loud four times**, because its sameness is the point and a class that invents a different question each time has not seen it. **Rows 3 are stoppings** — **the form hardest to produce and easiest to recognise.** **Rows 5 are the strongest on either card**: a count, a date and either _for the first time_ or a period. ⚠ **Row 1 of Card B is the one to stop on**: it is evidence and it is incomplete, and the listener who asks _out of how many?_ has done 4.5 without being told to.'));
out.push(S('Stage 4 · Your turn (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Claim from Stage 1: _I ask better questions on the telephone now._**',
  '**a** ⚠ **The occasion.** _On 19 June I rang the contractor and asked which office holds the delivery notes, and he had them in twenty minutes. In September I should have asked whether the notes existed._',
  '**b** ⚠ **My partner read only the occasion and said it was evidence of a different move: naming the document you want rather than asking whether a document exists.** **She is right and that is not the claim I made.** **The claim I made was about questions and the occasion is about documents** — **and I had not seen that the two are the same thing until she said so.**',
  '**And the entry as it now stands.** _On 19 June I asked for a named document rather than asking whether one existed. The move is 11.1 and I did not know I was using it on the telephone._',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['On the eleventh of June Mr Shihabi filed eighty-six words and the desk ran them unchanged, which had never happened before, and it has happened four times since and he can give the dates. Mrs Tarabishi said that is a result and not a move, and the move is what produced it and he did not notice doing it: he wrote the shape with the holes in it first, made two calls and filled them, and he had not decided to work that way but found that he had, about three weeks after he stopped thinking about it. Mrs Khoury said that is the only kind of evidence this cycle accepts, because a claim about yourself with no occasion behind it cannot be checked by anybody, including you, and I am more careful is true of everybody in the room every June and was true last June as well. Dr Qabbani said his is a negative, that nobody asked him something, and a negative with a date on it is the strongest evidence there is: in June a referee asked him nothing about his search, for the first time in four submissions, and four submissions is a denominator. Mrs Ajouz asked whether it is not strange to require a date about your own English, and Mrs Oueidat said it is exactly as strange as requiring one about anything else, which is to say not at all. Mr Tayara asked about somebody who genuinely has no occasion, and then nothing has become automatic yet and that is a true answer: a move can be learnt, usable and still deliberate. Mrs Rizk said hers is that she stopped doing something, and those are the best ones and the hardest to date, because nobody notices the day they stop — and the way to date a stopping is to find the last time you did it. Mr Attar asked how long a move takes to become automatic, and nobody in the class has reported less than two months or more than five, and the number depends on how often the occasion arises. Mr Zahreddine said he has written the same way for twenty years and three things are different. Mrs Tarabishi said hers is still deliberate every time, and Mrs Oueidat said that is the entry to write and not the one to be embarrassed by: she submits twice a year and the occasion has arisen twice, and a move made twice on purpose is a move. And Mr Shihabi said the thing he will take away is that he did not decide anything: the noticing came three weeks after the change, which means the change was not a decision and cannot be claimed as one.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The last line is the one to carry out of the cycle: the noticing came three weeks after the change, which means the change was not a decision and cannot be claimed as one.** **This is the sentence that makes every other claim in the unit believable** — **and a student who writes _I decided to start working this way_ about a change they noticed afterwards has written the one thing in the entry that is false.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(S('Board – the ten claims and what each one needs'));
out.push(A('⚠ **This is the board of 12.1a as it stood in this class, with the second column filled in afterwards and not at the time.** **Keep it for 12.2**, because four of the ten claims turn out to be items from the same students\' September lists.'));
out.push(table(['WHAT THE STUDENT SAID FIRST', 'WHAT IT NEEDED', 'WHAT IT BECAME'], [
  ['_I think about the reader more._', '**An occasion.** _When was the last time you did not?_', '_On 4 May I deleted "significant" before anybody asked me to._'],
  ['_I am much more careful._', '**An occasion.** ⚠ **The commonest feeling in the room and the emptiest.**', '_My last unchecked parameter is in a note of 14 March._'],
  ['_Nobody asked me about my search._', '**A denominator.** _Out of how many?_', '_For the first time in four submissions._'],
  ['_My formal English has improved._', '**An occasion, and the question is which document.**', '_Abandoned at Stage 4a. No occasion found._'],
  ['_I filed eighty-six words and they ran unchanged._', '⚠ **Nothing.** **A date, a count and a first time.**', '_Unchanged: 11 June, and four times since._'],
  ['_I stopped writing "kindly do the needful"._', '**The last instance.**', '_The last one is in a letter of March._'],
  ['_I understand hedging better._', '**An occasion.** ⚠ **Sounds technical and is a feeling.**', '_When did you last take a hedge out again?_ **No answer.**'],
  ['_Three letters have gone with no formula at the top._', '**Nothing.** **A count with a period.**', '_Three since April._'],
  ['_I am more confident with senior readers._', '**An occasion, and it is a 12.3 item.**', '_Moved to 12.3: the office has never refused one._'],
  ['_I read the body before the abstract now._', '**A date and a figure.**', '_10 May, eleven minutes, two sentences out._'],
], [2, 2, 2]));
out.push(A('**1** ⚠ **Four things, and three have dates.** **The fourth is the absences list for a story to be translated overnight** — **and it is listed as not yet automatic, because he has done it three times and each time because he remembered.**'));
out.push(A('**2** ⚠ **Because there was no decision to date it by.** **He noticed about three weeks after it started that he had stopped writing sentences first**, so the only datable thing is the result: the eighty-six words the desk ran unchanged on 11 June.'));
out.push(A('**3** ⚠ **Whether the change in the first item is about English at all.** **He has better questions to ask on the telephone than he had in September, and asking a better question in Arabic is not an improvement in English** — **and he says expressly that 12.3 is the cycle for it and that he has written nothing about it in the note.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 6 · Write with help (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**M. OUEIDAT** · _note for my own file_ · _three things that are different_ · **27 July**',
  '**Three things are different and two of them have dates.** ⚠ **The third has no occasion behind it yet and is listed as not yet automatic.**',
  '**One: I write the list of absences before the version.** **On 24 July I sent a covering note with three absences in it, which had not happened before.** **It has happened twice since: 29 July and 2 August.** ⚠ **I did not decide to work this way.**',
  '**Two: I have stopped reading the English version first.** **The last time I did is in a file of 11 May.** **A stopping is dated by its last instance.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 7 · Write freely (sample, 281 words)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**M. OUEIDAT** · _note for my own file_ · _four things that are different, with the occasions_ · **2 August**',
  '**Four things are different and three of them have dates.** ⚠ **The fourth has no occasion behind it and is listed as not yet automatic**, which is an entry and not a gap.',
  '**One: I write the list before the version.** **On 24 July a covering note went out with three absences in it and no summary of the document, which had not happened before in eleven years of summaries.** **It has happened twice since, on 29 July and 2 August.** ⚠ **I did not decide to do this.** **I noticed in July, reading two summaries side by side, that the second had a list in front of it** — **so the change is dated by the document and not by any decision, because there was none.**',
  '**Two: I have stopped reading the English version first.** **The last time is a file of 11 May.** **There have been nine since and the Arabic has been first in all nine.** **A stopping is dated by its last instance, because nobody notices the day they stop.**',
  '**Three, a negative, which is the one I value.** **No judge has asked me what a covering line means since 4 May.** **Before that I was asked about one in roughly one summary in three** — **and the one in three is the registry\'s figure and not mine: the clerk keeps a note of queries and I had never asked to see it.**',
  '**Four, which is not automatic.** **I can state a degree to a court that has heard the other side.** ⚠ **I have done it twice, on 4 May and 18 June, and both times because I remembered to.** **A move I remember to make is not automatic and I am not claiming it as one.**',
  '**And one thing that has not changed and that I expected to.** **I still cannot hold a hedge made of grammar across the two languages.** **One attempt, 6 July, two sentences, signed by nobody.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 7P · Respond (sample slip — band 2)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Reader:** ⚠ **the teacher who gets this student in September, who has four minutes and no other document.**',
  '**Absent:** **a date against the third thing.** **The entry says _no judge has asked me_ and gives no period** — **so the reader cannot tell whether that is since May or since 2019.**',
  '**Absent:** **the denominator for the negative is given as the registry\'s figure and the registry is not named as a document anybody could ask for.**',
  '⚠ **Present and worth saying so:** **the not-automatic entry, in those words.** **A note in which everything has become automatic is a note nobody reads twice.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 7R · Share'));
out.push(A('⚠ **The rise, every time, and the room will not believe this until it hears it.** **Have one student read their strongest claim twice** — **once with a rise at the end and once falling** — **and ask which version the room wanted to reassure.** **It is the rise.** **Then say why it matters: reassurance costs the claim its evidence, because a fact that has been agreed to is no longer a fact that was offered.** **Fall on the last three words and stop.** ⚠ **End the cycle on Mr Shihabi\'s sentence and do not add to it: the noticing came three weeks after the change.**'));

// ===================== 12.2 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('12.2  The list, nine months on'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **The lists are read aloud in full, in the order they were written, with no commentary and no explanation of any item.** **Write only the total number of items for each student on the board.** **In most classes the lists run between four and nine items.** **The no-commentary rule is the whole of the exercise**: a student who explains an item as they read it is marking it, and the marking is 12.2a\'s job and not 12.2\'s. ⚠ **Three or four students will have lost the list and read a reconstruction, marked as reconstructed** — **which is worth having, because a reconstructed list and a real one differ in a way the room can see and the reconstruction is always shorter and kinder.**'));
out.push(A('**b** Justified: **2** and **3**. ⚠ **Both name a document with a date and say what was done in it** — **section 4.6 of 2 May with nine findings at four degrees; the letter of 12 May with point 5 refused and the office named.** **1 and 5 are a feeling and a teacher\'s opinion.** **4 is the one to spend time on**: _I have not had to write one_ is not a crossing-off at all but the third state, **and a student who crosses it off goes into the second book with a hole they cannot see.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — ⚠ **a document, with a date, in which the thing was done**; and where no occasion has arisen the item stays on the list, unmarked.'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** **Nine items, four crossed off**, each with a document and a date against it, **and two of the remaining five have had no occasion at all.**   **2** ⚠ **That they are a third state and not a failure to move.** **Three states and not two** — **gone with a document, still there with an attempt, and no occasion, which is neither** — **and a list with two states on it is a list that has been wished at.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **Three states and not two is the finding of this cycle and the room will collapse it into two within ten minutes if it is not held to.** **Gone, with a document. Still there, with an attempt. No occasion, which is neither.** **Write the three on the board before the listening and point at them.** **The pressure comes from the students themselves**: nobody wants an unmarked item, and the no-occasion row looks like an admission. ⚠ **Say what it actually is: a statement about the student\'s work and not about their English** — **Mrs Tarabishi submits twice a year and has not had to write a proposal, and anything written against that item would be a claim about her job.** **In this class two of the ten had three or more no-occasion items and both were the students with the narrowest work, not the weakest English.**'));
out.push(NOTE('**The attempt described in figures is what makes a still-there item usable in Book 2, and this is the part to drill.** ⚠ _Three attempts, all between 380 and 420 words against a figure of 300_ **is a position on a scale.** _I find covering notes hard_ **is a mood.** **The first can be worked on in the second book; the second cannot be worked on by anybody.** **Make every still-there item carry a number**: attempts, words, how many were found by other people, how many by the student. ⚠ **And protect the striking-through.** **Two of Mrs Tarabishi\'s nine are items she would not now write at all** — _cannot write quickly_, _cannot sound like a native speaker_ — **and they are struck with the September hand legible underneath, not crossed off.** **It is the only place in Book 1 where a student is asked to disagree with themselves in writing, and the September hand has to stay readable or the disagreement has no second party.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** **Gone, with a document** — _cannot state a degree of certainty: chapter 4, section 4.6, written 2 May, nine findings at four degrees._   **2** **Still there, with the attempt** — _cannot write a covering note of the right length: three attempts, 380 to 420 words against a figure of 300._   **3** ⚠ **No occasion, unmarked** — _cannot write a proposal._ **Nothing written against it.**   **4** **Three items that are one move** — _cannot say how sure I am_, _cannot refuse a referee_ **and** _cannot put a limitation under its claim_ **are three symptoms of one thing, written as three because in September the thing was not visible.**   **5** ⚠ **Not about English, and say so** — _cannot write quickly_, **struck through rather than crossed off.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** **Mark accepted.** **A document, a date and what was done in it.**',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **Refused.** _I feel better about limitations_ **is a feeling.** **Question: _which document has a limitation under its claim, and what is its date?_**',
  '**Row 3** **Accepted.** **10 May, eleven minutes** — **and the eleven minutes is worth more than the date, because it is the figure that will be compared next year.**',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **Refused, and the hardest refusal on the card.** **A teacher\'s opinion is not a document.** **Question: _which mediation, and who were the two parties?_**',
  '**Row 5** **Accepted as a mark.** _Still there_ **with no attempt behind it is incomplete** — **ask for the attempt in figures: how many times, and what came back.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card B)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** **Mark accepted.** **The letter of 12 May, point 5, with the office named.**',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **Refused, and it is the third state and not a crossing-off.** _I have not had to write one_ **means no occasion.** **The item stays on the list, unmarked.**',
  '**Row 3** **Accepted.** **11 June, filed unchanged** — **and the _unchanged_ is the document, because the absence of a change is what is being claimed.**',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **Refused.** _I know about them now_ **is knowledge and not an occasion.** **Question: _how many calques have you found in your own writing, and how many did other people find?_**',
  '**Row 5** **Accepted as a mark, and correctly the third state.** **No occasion, unmarked** — **and nothing is to be written against it.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3R · Perform – listener task'));
out.push(A('**Rows 2 and 4 on both cards are refused and for two different reasons**, which is the distinction the listener has to make. ⚠ **Card A row 2 and Card B row 4 are feelings or knowledge, and the question asks for a document.** **Card A row 4 is a teacher\'s opinion.** **Card B row 2 is not a refusal at all but a misfiled third state** — **no occasion, and the item stays.** **Make the room say which of the three kinds each refusal is.** **Rows 5 on both cards are correctly marked**, and Card A\'s is incomplete rather than wrong: a still-there item with no attempt in figures cannot be used by anybody in September.'));
out.push(S('Stage 4 · Your turn (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Six items in September. Three gone, two still there, one with no occasion.**',
  '**Gone:** _cannot refuse a referee\'s point_ — **letter of 12 May, point 5, office named.** _cannot read my abstract against my body_ — **10 May, eleven minutes, two sentences out.** _cannot state a degree I would defend_ — **section 4.6 of 2 May.**',
  '**Still there:** _cannot find a calque in my own writing_ — **six found by other people, none by me.** _cannot write a covering note of 300 words_ — **three attempts, 380 to 420.**',
  '**No occasion:** _cannot write a proposal._ ⚠ **Unmarked.**',
  '**b** ⚠ **And the thing the list said about itself.** **Three of the six were one move.** **I wrote them as three in September because I could not see the thing they were symptoms of** — **and seeing it is worth more than the three crossings-off.**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 4R · Report (sample)'));
out.push(SAMPLE(['Mrs Tarabishi had nine items in her own handwriting and has crossed off four, each with a document against it and a date, and two of the remaining five have had no occasion at all, which is not the same as not having moved. Mrs Khoury said that distinction is the whole of the cycle: three states and not two — gone with a document, still there with an attempt, and no occasion, which is neither — and a list with two states on it is a list that has been wished at. Dr Qabbani asked which four went, and cannot state a degree of certainty, which is section 4.6 of 2 May with nine findings at four degrees; cannot refuse a referee\'s point, which is the letter of 12 May with point 5 refused and the office named; cannot write a limitation under its claim, which is chapter 4 of 18 May; and cannot read my own abstract against my body, which went on 10 May and took eleven minutes. Mrs Oueidat said that is a list of occasions and not of abilities, and it can be checked by anybody who asks to see the four documents, which nobody ever does and which is why it is worth writing. Mr Shihabi asked about the two with no occasion, and cannot write a proposal and cannot mediate between two colleagues in English: she has not had to do either, and they stay on the list unchanged and unmarked. Mr Tayara asked whether that is not simply an excuse, and Mrs Khoury said it would be if the list were a report to somebody, and it is a list to yourself whose only purpose is deciding what the second book has to do. Mrs Ajouz said hers has an item she cannot cross off and cannot leave, and Mrs Oueidat said that is 12.3. Mrs Rizk said her list was four items and three were the same thing. Mr Attar asked whether they should write a new list, and 12.5 writes it and it is not the same document. Mr Zahreddine said he did not write one in September because he thought the exercise was for the others, and Mrs Khoury said he should write it now, in September\'s words and marked as reconstructed, because a reconstructed list and a real one differ in a way that is itself worth knowing. And Mrs Tarabishi said the thing she will take away is her own handwriting: she read nine items aloud that she did not remember writing, and the one she was most worried about in September is the one she crossed off first.']));
out.push(A('⚠ **The last line is the one to carry out of the cycle: she read nine items aloud in her own handwriting that she did not remember writing, and the one she was most worried about in September is the one she crossed off first.** **Say it to the room.** **A class that hears it stops treating the September list as an embarrassment** — **and the students who lost theirs will feel the loss properly for the first time, which is useful before Book 2.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 5 · Read'));
out.push(S('Board – Mrs Tarabishi\'s nine items, as marked'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Put this on the board after the listening and not before, and leave the third column blank until the room has argued about the second.** **The argument is always the same**: two students will want the no-occasion items in the second column and one will want them in the first.'));
