out.push(A('⚠ **Ask only two questions round the room and write the two tallies on the board.** **One: did your reader talk about the writing at all?** **Two: how long was the silence?** **In this class seven of ten readers said nothing about the writing, and the silences ran from nothing to about two minutes with a median near one.** **Say the median.** **A student whose reader was silent for ninety seconds and who has not heard the figure will believe the page failed.** ⚠ **Then one sentence: about a third of readers say nothing for a minute and then ask a question about the content** — **so the instruction is to wait, and not to help, and the writers who helped have no result at all.**'));

// ===================== 12.5 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('12.5  The readiness page'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **Three rows and three columns, and nothing else on the sheet.** **The move as it is now; its harder version; and one question that can be asked in four seconds to find out whether it has become automatic.** **Say the limit before anybody starts**: a page with nine rows is a syllabus and is read once. **In this class the students who could name eleven moves wrote three rows and the afternoon went on the striking and the choosing**, which is where the work is and where it should be.'));
out.push(A('**b** Belong on the page: **2** and **4**. ⚠ **Both have all three columns** — **the move, the harder version on the axis of the reader\'s power, and a question with a behaviour in it.** **1, 3 and 5 are a declaration, a feeling and a weakness, and none of the three can be set as work by anybody.** **The one to stop on is 5**: _my weakest area is vocabulary_ **is the shape of readiness page every student has written before and it is the shape that is useless in September** — **because it names a territory and not a move, and a teacher cannot set a territory.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — ⚠ **three moves, each with its harder version and a question that tests whether it is automatic** — **and nothing else.**'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** ⚠ **Because a move you already have is not a thing to practise.** **The second book has to be given something to do** — **and the harder version of _name the absence_ is naming it in a document somebody else wrote, which she does four times a year and has never done well.**   **2** ⚠ **That it is the column that makes the page worth keeping, and that it is not _can I do this_** — **which is answered yes by everybody in July** — **but a question with a behaviour in it:** _do I write the list before the version?_'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **One axis for the harder version, and it is the reader\'s power.** **Not length, not a new genre, not more of it.** **State the degree to a reader who has already decided the other way; name the absence in a document you cannot alter; put the limitation under somebody else\'s claim.** **A harder version that is longer or in a different genre has made the move into a different move, and the second book then has nothing to build on.** **Say the axis, write it on the board, and refuse every row that gets harder in another direction.** ⚠ **The test of the question column is the words _without choosing_.** **Dr Qabbani\'s _do I state the degree without choosing it?_ is the right shape** — **a move you choose is a move you have, and a move you make without choosing is a move that has you** — **and that is the whole difference between a move learnt and a move automatic.**'));
out.push(S('Language box · Practise'));
out.push(A('**1** **A move with a document behind it** — _name the absence before the version (11.1), covering note of 24 July._   **2** **Its harder version, by the reader\'s power** — _name it in a document I did not write and cannot alter._   **3** **The question, with a behaviour in it** — _do I write the list before the version?_ ⚠ **Not _can I name an absence?_**   **4** ⚠ **One that belongs on the second sheet** — _the court will not accept a covering line unless the judge asks for it._ **The office is the registry and the document is a note to the registrar.**   **5** ⚠ **The move you talk about most** — **and the exercise is to check whether it has a document behind it.** **In this class it usually has not, which is how the selection rule proves itself.**'));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card A)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** **Complete and correct.** **Move, harder version by the reader\'s power, and a question with a behaviour in it.**',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **Does not belong on the page.** **It is the second sheet**: the office is the regional office and the document is a note with a date on it, **and the two question marks cannot be filled in because there is no move to make harder.**',
  '**Row 3** **Complete.** ⚠ **_Does the therefore arrive by itself?_ is the best question shape on either card** — **a behaviour, and one that cannot be answered yes out of politeness.**',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **Does not belong.** _I want to improve my vocabulary_ **is a territory and not a move.** **Nothing can be set against it** — **and the repair is to ask which document produced the want.**',
  '**Row 5** **Complete.** **The harder version is _to somebody senior_, which is the right axis** — **and the question has the test in it: do I apply the test before conceding?**',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3 · Practise (sample – Card B)'));
out.push(SAMPLE([
  '**Row 1** **Complete and correct.** ⚠ **_Without choosing_ is the phrase that makes the question a test of automatic and not of ability.**',
  '**Row 2** ⚠ **Does not belong.** **Second sheet: the office is the inspectorate and the document is a note naming the absence** — **which is 12.3 and was dealt with there.**',
  '**Row 3** **Complete.** **_With no telephone available_ is the reader\'s power expressed as the absence of help** — **and the question, _do I draft the holes first?_, is a behaviour.**',
  '**Row 4** ⚠ **Does not belong, and is the weakest thing on either card.** _My writing is better than it was_ **is a comparison with no move in it.** **Ask what document shows it.**',
  '**Row 5** **Complete.** ⚠ **_Do I read it aloud before sending?_ is the only question on either card that names a physical act**, which is why it is the easiest of the six to answer honestly.',
]));
out.push(S('Stage 3R · Perform – listener task'));
out.push(A('**Rows 2 and 4 on both cards do not belong on a readiness page and for two different reasons**, which is what the listener has to separate. ⚠ **Rows 2 are second-sheet items**: an office, a document and a date, and no move to make harder. **Rows 4 are territories and comparisons** — _I want to improve my vocabulary_, _my writing is better than it was_ — **with no move in them at all, and the question to put to each is which document produced it.** **Rows 1, 3 and 5 are complete.** **Make the room read the three questions aloud and say which has a behaviour in it**: all three do, and the phrases that carry the test are _without choosing_, _by itself_ and _before sending_.'));
out.push(S('Stage 4 · Your turn (sample)'));
