out.push(S('Stage 7R · Share'));
out.push(A('⚠ **Two numbers from each student and nothing else: how many moves they could name, and how many rows they kept.** **Write both columns on the board.** **In this class the first column has run between six and eleven and the second has been three for everybody, because three was the instruction.** **Then ask one question**: how many struck a move that had no document behind it? **Four of ten did, and all four said it was the unpleasant part.** ⚠ **Say why it is the part worth keeping: the two items Mrs Oueidat struck were both moves she believed she had** — **and a readiness page with nothing struck on it has not been chosen from anything.**'));

// ===================== 12.6 =====================
out.push(pb());
out.push(h2('12.6  The proposal for what you will do with it'));
out.push(S('Stage 1 · Get ready'));
out.push(A('**a** Open. ⚠ **The name goes on the board before anything is written, and it must be a person with a budget or a decision and not a department.** _My team lead, Firas Haddad_, **not** _the company_. **Then one question to each student: has that person ever been asked for anything by you?** **In this class seven of ten had never asked their named reader for anything at all**, and Mr Attar\'s two years is the figure to say out loud, because a proposal to somebody who has never heard from you is a different document from one to somebody who has.'));
out.push(A('**b** Belong: **2** and **5**. ⚠ **Both are about the reader\'s office in the reader\'s units** — **forty letters a month and three returned; two days a month in re-drafting on the office\'s own figures at annexe A.** **1, 3 and 4 are requests about the writer**, and the room should be made to say what each one asks the reader to care about. **The one to spend time on is 1**: _I would like to be given the opportunity_ **is the sentence almost every student writes first**, and it is refusable in four seconds because nothing in it belongs to the reader.'));
out.push(S('Stage 2 · Listen and read'));
out.push(A('**a** **B** — ⚠ **it is not a request about you**: it is about something the reader\'s office is paying for now, and the English is the instrument and not the subject.'));
out.push(A('**b** **1** **To draft the English release notes for six months, with whoever ships the release checking the technical content.** ⚠ **Firas Haddad, his team lead, has to agree to it** — **and has never been asked for anything by him in two years.**   **2** ⚠ **That the figure is the first paragraph.** **A proposal to somebody who has not agreed begins with what their office is paying for now** — **and not with the remedy, and never with the writer** — **and she says she has been making the same mistake for eleven years.**'));
out.push(NOTE('⚠ **The ask goes once, in the middle, in one sentence, and the model says so about itself: _one sentence, and it is the only thing asked for in this document_.** **A proposal with the ask in the first paragraph and again in the last has told a budget holder four times that somebody wants something** — **and a want can be refused in four seconds, whereas a figure has to be answered.** **Count the asks in every draft and write the number on the paper.** **In this class the first drafts carried between two and five asks and nobody had written one.** ⚠ **And the failure condition is the sentence that decides it.** _If the figure has not moved by March, the arrangement ends._ **Writers put it in last and reluctantly, and in this class it is the sentence that got half the proposals granted** — **because a six-month arrangement with no end in it is a permanent change, and a reader who has been handed the exit does not have to invent one.**'));
out.push(A('**The hardest line in the genre is the one about English, and it has to be said in 12.6 or half the class writes the wrong document.** ⚠ **The word _English_ appears about once in a good proposal of this kind and not in the first paragraph.** **Nowhere does Mr Attar\'s proposal say that his English has improved**, and his last paragraph says why: the four wrong sentences are wrong in their facts, **and a note with a correct parameter in clumsy English costs nobody a ticket.** **Dr Qabbani will ask whether the English comes into it at all** — **it is the instrument and not the subject, and saying so is what makes the proposal readable by somebody who does not care how anybody writes.** ⚠ **And refuse the larger ask.** **Mr Attar does not propose a named owner in the process document**: it would outlast six months and needs the document opened, which is the reader\'s decision and not a thing the writer can offer to do. **A proposal that asks for the larger change as well is refused on the larger one.**'));
