out.push(NOTE('⚠ **This is the twelfth and last mediation in Book 1 and the two parties are the same person, which is what makes it the hardest of the twelve.** **The three things, in this order and nothing else: what September was right about; what September had no way of knowing; and the one thing now available that was not.** **No verdict, and no encouragement.** **The order matters as much as the content** — **it is 7.2\'s concession at the strongest point, arriving for the last time, and a note in that order is read to the end by its own writer in November.** ⚠ **The commonest failure is a note that is kind, which is not the same as a note that is an account.** **_September could not have known_ is an account.** **_September should have known_ is a reproach and is also false**: the evidence September needed was in a day-book nobody had asked for. **The distinction is one word and the room should be made to say both sentences aloud.**'));
